.TH CBMAP_INSERT_ELEM 3 "2026-07-10" "c_collections" "C Collections Library - Functions"
.SH NAME
cbmap_insert_elem \- insert a key-value pair into the BST map
.SH LIBRARY
C Collections (libccollections, \-lccollections)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
#include <cbstmap.h>

ccol_retval_t cbmap_insert_elem(cbmap cbm,
                                 const cmap_pair *key_pair,
                                 const cmap_pair *val_pair);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.nf
Inserts a key-value pair into the BST map. If the key already exists,
the old value is replaced. Tree is automatically rebalanced using AVL
rotations after insertion.
.fi
.SH PARAMETERS
.nf
cbm        BST map to insert into
key_pair   Key to insert (copied into map)
val_pair   Value to associate with key (copied into map)
.fi
.SH RETURN VALUE
.nf
ccol_success               - New key inserted successfully
ccol_key_already_present   - Key already existed; value updated successfully
ccol_container_full        - Map has reached max_elem_count
ccol_not_enough_memory     - Memory allocation failed
.fi
.SH NOTES
.nf
O(log n) complexity
Key and value data are copied into the map
If key exists, old value is freed and replaced
.fi
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR cbmap_insert (3),
.BR cbmap_delete_elem (3),
.BR cbmap_get_elem_ref (3)
